Handling Jenkins Pipeline Failures
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand different types of Jenkins pipeline failures and their causes
Implement retry mechanisms with exponential backoff for transient failures in Jenkins pipelines
Configure Jenkins pipelines to send email notifications on build failure
Create robust, reusable error handling strategies in Jenkins declarative pipelines using shared helper functions
Implement a deploy-with-rollback pattern that validates deployments via health checks
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Jenkins and CI/CD concepts
Familiarity with Jenkins declarative pipeline syntax
Basic knowledge of Linux command line operations
Understanding of Git version control system
Completion of an introductory Jenkins lab or equivalent experience
This lab is performed entirely on a self-owned, isolated practice machine (such as the Al Nafi cloud lab environment) so that pipeline failure handling and rollback logic can be studied safely without affecting any production system.

